survivors.evidence:
The sitemap is built from a HAND-MAINTAINED list:

  const PAGES = ['/', '/roadmap.html', '/releases.html', '/feedback.html', '/geez.html',
    '/about-the-geez-bible.html', '/ethiopian-bible-canon.html', '/copy-the-bible-text.html']
    .concat(readerUrls.sort());

but pages are auto-discovered by walkHtml() and tracked in `builtPages`. The list omits `/how-to-use.html`, which the build actually emits (dist/how-to-use.html, 21 KB), carries a self-referential canonical (`<link rel="canonical" href="https://www.yhwhyaway.com/how-to-use.html">` — i.e. it is meant to be indexed), sits in the global nav of every page (head.html: `<a href="{{root}}how-to-use.html" data-nav="how-to">Guide</a>`), and is linked inbound from all 10 top-level pages. `grep -c how-to-use website/dist/sitemap.xml` = 0. The list also predates the Guide page, so it will keep drifting: every future top-level src/*.html page silently misses the sitemap too. (beta.html and 404.html are correctly absent — beta.html's canonical points to releases.html and 404.html is an error page.)
